            "reviewBody": "In need of an inexpensive, multimedia card reader since I work with various devices and require to transfer between them. After comparing this one with the Inland card reader, I decided to give this one a shot as it appeared and felt better quality, up close. Installation was a hassle with the converter bay because the screws didn't fit. The software booted and installed on its own once it had connected to the mobo. Every slot works and detects any memory card when inserted. One thing I will note is that it's somewhat slower than my old HP desktop's card reader. Another thing I dislike is the blue light aka Power that glows on the left hand side (the image shown is upside down). The Power stays on, proudly, whether the pc is on or off. Overall, this card reader works, there's just nothing really fancy. Hence the 3-star rating.",
